From 983203a03cb4457bef4a136b8813cc70866298f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:11:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Test real complete-block reorg recovery and source
 restoration

Embed immutable full-wire vectors generated with the existing explicit development manifest and Python reference revision 82e7135016aaf6b6d6d191a7422348016f72984f. Record manifest and scratch-generator digests beside the vectors; no profile defaults or issuance changes are introduced.

Validate both divergent branches through the native complete-block oracle against independent CoinEntry, UTXO root and monetary expectations before using actual development-chain disk connects. Cover two source detaches and three replacement attaches, invalid-middle replacement rollback and exact source restoration, high-time ancestor clock rollback, reopen after every durable step, touched-coin proofs and H/A/I/S agreement, pending writer fences and preparation/resume capacity refusal.

The standalone Debug suite passes against the coherent storage, connector and coordinator drafts. These are module recovery checks, not daemon or socket integration claims; lower-level crash and ambiguous-sync fault injection belongs to the storage suite.
---
